ata><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KARLSRUHE FORSCHZENT</name><address><country>DE</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI ELECTRIC CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA HAJIME</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>RUTHER PATRICK</name><address><country>DE</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FORSCHUNGSZENTRUM KARLSRUHE GMBH</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA, HAJIME</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>RUTHER, PATRICK</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA HAJIME</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>RUTHER PATRICK</name><address><country>DE</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAJIMA, HAJIME</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>RUTHER, PATRICK</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A lens for converting an optical axis, comprising a plane of incidence (1a) which the outgoing light from a flat light introducing body (2) enters, a columnar lens surface (1d) which has an optical axis (C) in a position or a direction different from that of an optical axis (A) of the light entering the plane of incidence (1a), and which is adapted to condense the light in the direction of the optical axis (C), an inner reflector (1b) adapted to convert the optical axis (A) of the incident light entering the plane of incidence (1a) into an optical axis (B), and a second inner reflector (1c) adapted to convert the optical axis (B) into the optical axis (C), thereby enabling the optical axis (A) to be converted into the optical axis (B, C) without being restricted by the height of the flat light introducing body (2), and a narrow beam to be formed even in a position far away from the flat light introducing body (2).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une lentille servant à modifier un axe optique, qui comporte un plan d'incidence (1a) par lequel pénètre la lumière sortant d'un corps (2) d'introduction de lumière plat; une surface (1d) de lentille colonnaire présentant un axe optique (C) se trouvant dans une position ou orientation différente de celle d'un axe optique (A) de lumière pénétrant le plan d'incidence (1a), et qui est conçue pour concentrer la lumière en direction de l'axe optique (C); un réflecteur interne (1b) conçu pour modifier l'axe optique (A) de lumière incidente pénétrant le plan d'incidence (1a) en un axe optique (B); et un deuxième réflecteur (1c) interne conçu pour modifier l'axe optique (B) en l'axe optique (C). Ce système permet de modifier l'axe optique (A) en l'axe optique (B, C) sans être limité par la hauteur du corps (2) d'introduction de lumière plat, et de former un faisceau étroit même dans une position très éloignée du corps (2) d'introduction de lumière plat.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>